{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.sumRule_mirror_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.sumRule_mirror_difference","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChargeRule.lean#L179-L184","doc":"The sum rule's mirror difference at fixed `A` is `(A-1)(Z - W)` — also\nnonzero, which is why the model *has* a mirror splitting at all, and flat in the\nsense that its `Z`-dependence carries no extra factor of `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.prodRule_mirror_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.prodRule_mirror_difference","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChargeRule.lean#L170-L177","doc":"Under the product rule a mirror pair `(Z, ·)` vs `(W, ·)` at fixed `A`\ndiffers by `(Z - W)(Z + W - 1)`, i.e. `(Z-W)(A-1)` for a mirror pair where\n`Z + W = A`. **Linear in `A`.** The observed Coulomb displacement energy goes as\n`(A-1)/A^{1/3}`, so the product rule fixes the multiplicity and still lacks the\n`1/R` of a Coulomb energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.no_scaling_of_sumRule_is_prodRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.no_scaling_of_sumRule_is_prodRule","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChargeRule.lean#L154-L166","doc":"**No multiple of the sum-rule total is the product-rule total.** Over `ℤ`,\nwhere `2 ≠ 0`; the coefficient is chosen first, so the whole family is excluded\nat once. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.prodRuleTotalDoubled_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.prodRuleTotalDoubled_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChargeRule.lean#L146-L152","doc":"The product-rule total is **quadratic**: its second difference is the nonzero\nconstant `2`. So no rescaling of the sum rule can reproduce it — this is the\ndegree gap `CrossingCountAffine` states, traced to its source. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.sumRuleTotal_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.sumRuleTotal_affine","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChargeRule.lean#L140-L144","doc":"The sum-rule total is **affine** in `Z` at fixed `A`: its second difference\nvanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.prodRuleTotalDoubled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.prodRuleTotalDoubled","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChargeRule.lean#L136-L138","doc":"**The product rule totals to `Z(Z-1)/2`** — the number of proton pairs.\nStated doubled, to stay division-free over a bare `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.sumRuleTotal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.sumRuleTotal","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChargeRule.lean#L132-L134","doc":"**The sum rule totals to `(A-1)·Z`** — each nucleon appears in `A-1` bonds,\nso `Σ_{i<j} (Qᵢ + Qⱼ) = (A-1)·Σᵢ Qᵢ = (A-1)Z`. Linear in `Z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.prodRule_like_pairs_are_strong_baseline","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.prodRule_like_pairs_are_strong_baseline","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChargeRule.lean#L119-L124","doc":"Under the product rule the neutron pair sits exactly on the mixed-charge\nbaseline, so the **strong** channel is charge-symmetric and the only charge\ndependence left is on `pp` — which is what an electromagnetic term should be. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.sumRule_like_pairs_differ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.sumRule_like_pairs_differ","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChargeRule.lean#L113-L117","doc":"The sum rule makes the two **like** pairs differ by `2c` — charge-odd across\n`p ↔ n`, which is `qou-1pig`'s measured defect (`f_pp - f_nn = h = 2·(h/2)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.rules_differ_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.rules_differ_nn","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChargeRule.lean#L107-L111","doc":"**On a neutron pair they differ by `c`.** The sum rule charges two neutral\nobjects `-c`; the product rule charges them `0`. This one bond is the whole\ndisagreement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.rules_agree_pn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.rules_agree_pn","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChargeRule.lean#L103-L105","doc":"On a mixed pair both rules give `0` — the baseline. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.rules_agree_pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.rules_agree_pp","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChargeRule.lean#L99-L101","doc":"On a proton pair both rules give `+c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.prodRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.prodRule","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChargeRule.lean#L91-L93","doc":"**The Coulomb rule**: the *product* of the two charges, times `c`. Two\nobjects interact electromagnetically in proportion to `Qᵢ·Qⱼ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.sumRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChargeRule.sumRule","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChargeRule.lean#L86-L89","doc":"**The implemented rule**: the centred *sum* of the two charges, times the\nper-crossing correction `c = h/2`. Measured to be exactly what\n`interface_factor` produces. ","signatureChunk":0}]}